<div class="pd-toggleswitch-documentation">

	<section id="overview">
		<h2 class="doc-section">Overview</h2>
		<p>
			<code>PDToggleSwitch</code> is a boolean toggle switch component for on/off states.
			Provides a more visual alternative to checkboxes, with optional on/off labels inside
			the switch, rounded corners, three sizes, and full CSS variable theming.
		</p>
		<ul>
			<li><strong>Sizes</strong> — Small, Medium, Large</li>
			<li><strong>Labels</strong> — optional text inside the switch and/or an external label</li>
			<li><strong>Rounded</strong> — pill-shaped toggle via <code>Rounded="true"</code></li>
			<li><strong>Theming</strong> — CSS variable support via <code>--pd-toggle-*</code></li>
		</ul>
	</section>

	<section id="quick-start">
		<h2 class="doc-section">Quick Start</h2>

		<DocExample Title="Basic Toggle"
					AnchorId="basic-toggle"
					Code="@_example1Code"
					Language="razor"
					DemoStyle="min-height: 80px;">
			<DemoContent>
				<div class="d-flex align-items-center gap-3">
					<PDToggleSwitch @bind-Value="_isEnabled" Label="Enable Feature" />
					<span class="text-muted">Value: @_isEnabled</span>
				</div>
			</DemoContent>
			<Description>
				<p>
					Bind to a <code>bool</code> with <code>@@bind-Value</code>. Use <code>Label</code> for an external text label.
				</p>
			</Description>
		</DocExample>

		<DocExample Title="With On/Off Text"
					AnchorId="onoff-text"
					Code="@_example2Code"
					Language="razor"
					DemoStyle="min-height: 80px;">
			<DemoContent>
				<PDToggleSwitch @bind-Value="_isEnabled" OnText="ON" OffText="OFF" Rounded="true" />
			</DemoContent>
			<Description>
				<p>
					Use <code>OnText</code> and <code>OffText</code> to display labels inside the switch track.
					<code>Rounded="true"</code> gives a pill shape.
				</p>
			</Description>
		</DocExample>
	</section>

	<section id="parameters">
		<h2 class="doc-section">Parameters</h2>
		<table class="table table-sm doc-props-table">
			<thead>
				<tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr>
			</thead>
			<tbody>
				<tr><td><code>Value</code></td><td><code>bool</code></td><td>false</td><td>Current on/off state</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>ValueChanged</code></td><td><code>EventCallback&lt;bool&gt;</code></td><td>—</td><td>Fired when the switch is toggled; use with <code>@@bind-Value</code></td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>Label</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td>""</td><td>External text label rendered alongside the switch</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>LabelBefore</code></td><td><code>bool?</code></td><td>false</td><td>Place the label before (left of) the switch</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>OnText</code></td><td><code>string?</code></td><td>null</td><td>Text displayed inside the switch when on</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>OffText</code></td><td><code>string?</code></td><td>null</td><td>Text displayed inside the switch when off</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>TextCssClass</code></td><td><code>string?</code></td><td>null</td><td>Additional CSS classes applied to the SVG text element (useful for font weight, size, or custom colour)</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>Rounded</code></td><td><code>bool?</code></td><td>false</td><td>Render the switch with pill-shaped (fully rounded) ends</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>Width</code></td><td><code>int?</code></td><td>auto</td><td>Override the switch width in pixels</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>Height</code></td><td><code>int?</code></td><td>auto</td><td>Override the switch height in pixels</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>BorderWidth</code></td><td><code>int?</code></td><td>2</td><td>Width of the switch border in pixels</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>Options</code></td><td><code>PDToggleSwitchOptions</code></td><td>new()</td><td>Options object for setting defaults; individual parameters take precedence</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>IsEnabled</code></td><td><code>bool</code></td><td>true</td><td>Enable or disable the switch</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>CssClass</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td>""</td><td>Additional CSS classes on the root element</td></tr>
			</tbody>
		</table>
	</section>

	<section id="options">
		<h2 class="doc-section">PDToggleSwitchOptions</h2>
		<p>
			Pass a <code>PDToggleSwitchOptions</code> instance to <code>Options</code> to share settings
			across multiple switches. Any directly set parameter overrides the corresponding option.
		</p>
		<table class="table table-sm doc-props-table">
			<thead>
				<tr><th>Property</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr>
			</thead>
			<tbody>
				<tr><td><code>OnText</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td>""</td><td>Default on text</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>OffText</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td>""</td><td>Default off text</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>TextCssClass</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td>""</td><td>Default CSS classes for the SVG text element</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>Rounded</code></td><td><code>bool</code></td><td>false</td><td>Default rounded setting</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>LabelBefore</code></td><td><code>bool</code></td><td>false</td><td>Default label position</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>Size</code></td><td><code>ButtonSizes</code></td><td>Medium</td><td>Default size: Small, Medium, or Large</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>BorderWidth</code></td><td><code>int</code></td><td>2</td><td>Default border width in pixels</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>Width</code></td><td><code>int?</code></td><td>null</td><td>Default width override</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>Height</code></td><td><code>int?</code></td><td>null</td><td>Default height override</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>CssClass</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td>""</td><td>Default additional CSS classes</td></tr>
			</tbody>
		</table>
	</section>

	<section id="css-variables">
		<h2 class="doc-section">CSS Variables</h2>
		<p>
			Set these variables on a parent element or directly via <code>style</code> on a wrapper
			<code>&lt;div&gt;</code> to override colours without writing component-specific CSS.
		</p>
		<table class="table table-sm doc-props-table">
			<thead>
				<tr><th>Variable</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr>
			</thead>
			<tbody>
				<tr><td><code>--pd-toggle-on-color</code></td><td>--bs-primary (#1b6ec2)</td><td>Fill and stroke colour of the switch in the on state</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>--pd-toggle-off-color</code></td><td>#adb5bd</td><td>Fill and stroke colour of the switch in the off state</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>--pd-toggle-on-text-color</code></td><td>white</td><td>Colour of the on-state text inside the switch</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>--pd-toggle-off-text-color</code></td><td>white</td><td>Colour of the off-state text inside the switch</td></tr>
			</tbody>
		</table>
		<p>Example — custom colours via a wrapper div:</p>
		<pre><code>&lt;div style="--pd-toggle-on-color: #198754; --pd-toggle-off-color: #dc3545;"&gt;
    &lt;PDToggleSwitch OnText="YES" OffText="NO" Rounded="true" /&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>
	</section>

</div>
